    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "How Fatigue Sets In",
      "items": [
        "Too many alerts cause important alerts to be missed",
        "Each missed incident tends to add reactive alerts",
        "The extra noise feeds the next round of ignored alerts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Prevention Strategies",
      "items": [
        "Threshold adjustment: do not set overly sensitive thresholds",
        "Alert grouping and inhibition: bundle related alerts, suppress child alerts",
        "Regular review and gradual introduction: remove unneeded alerts, start new ones at low severity"
